course: dictionary
lesson: 12845
title: Encryption: secret codes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Encryption means turning a message into a secret code so that nobody else can read it. The message is scrambled, and only someone with the right key can unscramble it. Clue words like secret, code and key tell you the message is hidden.
explain: «The app uses encryption to keep your messages private.» Private means only you and your friend can read them. So encryption must be a way of hiding messages from everyone else. Test it: put «secret code» in place of encryption and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Without the key, the scrambled message is just nonsense.» The key is what unlocks the code. When you see scrambled, secret or key near a word, check whether the word is about hiding information.
fact: Encryption means turning a message or data into a secret code.
fact: Only someone with the right key can read an encrypted message.
fact: The padlock in a web browser means the connection uses encryption.
fact: «Encryption» can also mean one particular system of making codes, so you might say «strong encryption».
fact: In history, code-breakers at Bletchley Park worked to break the encryption of the Enigma machine.
exercise: «The app uses encryption to keep your messages private.» What does encryption do here? | *It turns messages into a secret code | It sends messages to everyone | It makes the messages louder | It deletes every message
exercise: «Without the key, the scrambled message is just nonsense.» What is the key for? | To print the message | *To unlock the secret code | To open a front door | To make the message longer
exercise: What does the padlock in a web browser tell you? | The page has no pictures | The page is only for children | *The connection uses encryption | The computer is locked and cannot be used
test: «Only someone with the right key can read an encrypted message.» Who can read it? | *Someone with the right key | Your teacher's phone | Anyone who can see the screen | Someone with a faster internet
test: «Our bank uses strong encryption to protect your money.» What does strong encryption mean here? | A very fast computer | *A very good secret code that is hard to break | A heavy metal box | A very loud noise
exam: «Encryption keeps passwords and bank details safe when they travel across the internet.» What is encryption mainly for? | Printing documents | Playing games | Making the internet faster | *Keeping private information safe
